# Milestone: M3
# Covers: tag.stop() terminates execution within the tagged block;
#         code after the tagged block does not run.
#
# defer-to: T29
#
# Reason: requires UTag as a real runtime type and OP_TAG_STOP absorption in
# the unwind walker.  Both land at T29 (UTag + ambient-tag inheritance helpers).
# At M3, OP_PUSH_TAG/OP_POP_TAG are emitted as stubs but OP_TAG_STOP has no
# runtime absorption — UEXEC_TAG_STOP escalates to fatal rather than being
# caught by a matching TAG_SCOPE entry.
#
# When T29 lands, implement this fixture by uncommenting the urbiscript source
# below.  Expected behaviour: "before" is printed; "after" is NOT printed
# because tag.stop() terminates the tagged block.
#
# Urbiscript source (activate at T29):
#   var t = Tag.new;
#   t: { echo("before"); t.stop(); echo("after") };
#   echo("done")
#   --- expected output ---
#   [00000001] "before"
#   [00000002] "done"
